  "what_each_count_counts": "`independent_draws_this_book` is the number of households whose elasticity the priced leg re-rolled, and it is the ONLY sample size here: the draw is a pure function of (customer_id, seed), so it is what 1/n indexes. `priced_decisions_this_book` counts renewal decisions, and the decisions on one account share one draw. `elasticity_calls_per_seed` counts CALL SITES -- re-reads of the same draws -- and is a sample size for nothing at all. `times_this_book` is invariant across all three; the absolute counts are not.",
